  "question": {
    "text": "The refractive index of a transparent liquid filled in an equilateral hollow prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>. The angle of minimum deviation for the liquid will be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "30",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For minimum deviation in a prism,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>The value of minimum deviation is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
